Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) 

What the data looks like
Any patterns or imbalances
Missing values or outliers
Relationships between features and the target


d EDA and feature engineering, 

one-hot encoding 


 Decision Tree Classifier
A simple, intuitive model that splits the data based on feature values.
✅ Pros:
Easy to understand and visualize
Works well with both categorical and numerical data
No need for feature scaling
❌ Cons:
Prone to overfitting
Can be unstable with small data changes


Random Forest Classifier
An ensemble of decision trees — builds many trees and averages their results.
✅ Pros:
Reduces overfitting by averaging
Handles missing values and outliers well
Feature importance built-in
❌ Cons:
Slower than a single tree
Harder to interpret


🔥 3. Gradient Boosting (e.g. GradientBoostingClassifier, XGBoost, LightGBM)
Builds trees sequentially, each trying to correct the previous one.
✅ Pros:
Often state-of-the-art accuracy
Can model complex patterns
Robust to overfitting with tuning
❌ Cons:
Slower to train
Requires careful tuning


📈 4. Logistic Regression
A linear model that predicts probabilities (used for binary classification).
✅ Pros:
Simple and fast
Interpretable coefficients
Great baseline model
❌ Cons:
Assumes linearity
Needs numeric input (use one-hot encoding)
Not good for complex or nonlinear data

